.TH XIL\-DB\-PROFILE "1" "2026\-07\-02" "xil\-pipeline 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xil\-db\-profile \- profile MP3 audio levels: peak, average, and minimum dBFS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xil\-db\-profile
[\-h] [\fI\,PATH\/\fR] [\-\-output FILE] [\-\-absolute] [\-\-json]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Recursively scans a directory (or a single MP3 file) and reports the peak,
average (RMS), and minimum dBFS loudness for each file.  Useful for
normalisation auditing before assembly or mastering.
.PP
When
.I PATH
is omitted, scans the shared
.B SFX/
directory under the current workspace root.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I PATH
Directory or MP3 file to scan (default: \fI<workspace>\fR/SFX/)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Write results to FILE instead of stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-absolute\fR
Print absolute file paths (default: relative to scan root)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output a JSON array to stdout \(em no banner, safe to pipe to jq
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Profile the SFX library:
.B xil db\-profile
.TP
Profile a single episode's stems:
.B xil db\-profile stems/the413/S01E01 \-\-json
.TP
Save a CSV\-compatible report to a file:
.B xil db\-profile \-\-output loudness.txt
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xil (1),
.BR xil\-assemble (1),
.BR xil\-master (1),
.BR xil\-sfx\-lib (1)
.SH AUTHOR
John Brissette <xilcmd@gmail.com>
